    18	## Maintenance rules
    19	
    20	Authority: Alex's instructions, then `docs/DECISIONS.md`, then the PRDs and design page. If a PRD contradicts a decision, correct the PRD.
    21	
    22	After **every change**, reason through every module in this order: research universe → classification → Config → dispatch → extraction → thesis library → final verdict → pull mode → human review pool → system overview. Compare each with the decisions and ask:
    23	
    24	1. Does this change affect the module?
    25	2. Do its page and PRD describe the same behaviour?
    26	3. Do the examples still work?
    27	4. Do the acceptance criteria or open questions need to change?
    28	
    29	Correct inconsistencies and list what changed and why. Update decisions and current state in the same slice.
    30	
    31	Run `python3 docs/check.py` **last**. It compares generated PRD blocks with page data, rebuilds the bundle used when the page opens from disk, runs the classification simulation and checks rendering. It reports mismatches rather than correcting their meaning. A pass is a mechanical result, not the reasoning review.
     1	# Build a fresh English thesis library
     2	
     3	Decision: D163. Alex chose a fresh English library on October 25, 2026. Start with the original source documents and an empty ledger. Keep the existing Chinese library as historical evidence. This page owns the build sequence; the [English conversion plan](plan.md) owns language compatibility.
     4	
     5	For example, an NVIDIA earnings call should produce an English question, its English outcome ladder and English evidence summaries directly. The exact quotation remains the sentence in the earnings call. A later Reuters article is compared with the theses already written by earlier items; it can add evidence, repeat an existing source, or propose another question.
     6	
     7	## How the old library was made
     8	
     9	1. The corpus harvesters collected filings, earnings calls, company releases, official material and news pages. `assemble.py` put original text, publication dates, source identity, categories, subject labels and copy links into `items.sqlite`. A provider summary alone was not an original article eligible for extraction.
    10	2. The POC used the smaller `poc/data/items-window.sqlite`, not every item in the full corpus. Earlier NVIDIA company documents seeded the empty library from February 25 through July 23. The news replay began July 24. The initial source database included attachments subsequently marked as not material; `items-window-tags2-2026-10-24.sqlite` preserves the same source rows with corrected labels.
    11	3. `testdb.feed` read original items and copy records in publication-day order, company material before official material before news within a day. `dispatch.route` applied its existing completeness, copy, category and research-universe rules.
    12	4. Extraction read each original with the existing thesis context. It proposed complete questions and outcome ladders, plus evidence linked to existing or proposed theses. The role explicitly required Chinese generated text. Matching searched existing theses and evidence; writing stored the decisions, original quotations, source links, dependencies and successors in an append-only SQLite ledger.
    13	5. Judgement wrote the state and its evidence-backed reasons. The final UI library used per-item judgement until July 28 and daily judgement from July 29. Due theses were frozen and closed. This mixed cadence is historical, not the new build configuration.
    14	6. The sealed August 15 ledger feeds the API by default. `mock_data.py` also exported it for the early UI; `mock_translate.py` translated display strings afterwards, retaining Chinese `condition_zh` fields to read score direction. That export did not turn the underlying library into English.
    15	
    16	The UI ledger, later keyed trial ledgers and the latest adopted code are different things. The UI's sealed ledger was built with `poc-v2`; `poc-v16` incorporates later identity/reference fixes, and D159 changed replay to finish each item's writes before extracting the next. No default configuration currently implements D149 grouping.
    17	
    18	## Selected inputs and stages
    19	
    20	The first build uses the corrected, fixed POC source population in `poc/data/items-window-tags2-2026-10-24.sqlite`. It does not silently switch to the much larger `poc/corpus/items.sqlite`. `audit_library.py` records their actual sizes, selected input IDs, original-content hashes, route decisions and the difference from the UI library's source labels. Counts come from its output, not a hand-maintained target.
    21	
    22	| Stage | Inputs | Result and exit condition |
    23	|---|---|---|
    24	| Prepare, free | Existing source databases and ledgers | Record source provenance and exact populations; inspect hash/date/body failures before any model calls. No source or old ledger is rewritten. |
    25	| Complete English runtime, free | Adopted extraction/matching/judgement/Idea contracts | Activate new versioned English prompts only after canonical fields, complete request builders, periods, score orientation, source preservation and legacy reads pass their checks. Update preflight's request parsing and enum checks for English requests; its current Chinese-header parser cannot replay them. Keep provider/model/reasoning unchanged. |
    26	| Small paired check, proposed | The first NVIDIA results package and a later update from the recorded source list | Compare fresh old-language and English calls, at least three samples per arm. Agree the semantic expectations and an explicit cost cap before launching. No cached answers as model controls. |
    27	| Seed the English library | The 20 eligible earlier NVIDIA documents, in their existing chronological order | Write a new English ledger and call archive. Review omissions, duplicates, false merges, quantities, periods, citations and score direction. Stop on a failed registered acceptance. |
    28	| Continue the same ledger | July 24–31 from the fixed POC source population | Exercise updates against existing English theses, repeated-source handling, replacements and daily judgements. Do not reset the ledger between days. |
    29	| Extend and expose | August 1–15 after the smaller stages pass | Use a new search index and point the API/UI at the English ledger explicitly. Export directly; no display-translation job or dependency on `condition_zh`. |
    30	
    31	The small comparison is proposed, not launched or registered by this document. Its exact source IDs, semantic reading and cap must be settled before it becomes an acceptance. A source inventory proves input identity and routing, not correct extraction. A translated prompt or passing schema is likewise not evidence of model quality.
    32	
    33	Research reference lists remain hints: a topic outside a company's list can still be proposed. Preserving that D155 behavior is separate from supplying D149 research groups. The English baseline must not be presented as the finished grouping product. No failed two-step extraction arm is introduced through the language switch.
    34	
    35	## Inputs, outputs and transitions
    36	
    37	| State × event | Action and date |
    38	|---|---|
    39	| Preparation × original source read | Read SQLite with `mode=ro`; record existing input IDs, publication days and hashes. No model calls. |
    40	| Preparation × missing database, empty selected stage, inconsistent body hash or invalid date | Refuse preparation; do not substitute another corpus or call the model to discover what failed. |
    41	| Empty English ledger × first source | Use the source's publication day and dispatch sequence; propose English theses without importing old Chinese theses. |
    42	| Populated English ledger × next source | Finish the preceding write first; read the resulting English thesis context, then extract and match. |
    43	| End of day × changed theses | One dependency-ordered judgement round, then the existing due-date close step; record the completed day. |
    44	| Running × crash/refusal | Retain raw answers and completed writes; use existing resume behavior with the same pinned source/configuration. No reset or fresh sampling disguised as resume. |
    45	| Historical Chinese ledger × English build | Read only for comparison; never a target of the new run. |
    46	| Staged acceptance × failure | Record the failed population and trace; do not continue into the larger stage or change the standard to pass. |
    47	
    48	| Value × writer | Readers and contract |
    49	|---|---|
    50	| Source text, ID, date, source URI and hash × existing corpus | Extraction, original-quote checks, evidence source lookup, audit. Retain byte content and dates. |
    51	| English question, focus, outcome conditions and summary × versioned model requests | Matching, ledger, service, UI. Canonical vocabulary follows the PRD; source quotations are exempt from translation. |
    52	| Numeric bounds and period × extraction plus existing checks | Identity matching, succession, claim evaluation, chart orientation. Language must not change values or financial period. |
    53	| Run configuration and source population × build operator | Replay and verification. Use explicit separate source, views, archive and index paths; do not inherit the old CLI's `poc-v1` or API's sealed-library defaults. |
    54	| Preparation manifest × `audit_library.py` | Review and later run registration. It contains source references, not a second corpus or generated theses. |
    55	
    56	| New path × old checks | Required evidence |
    57	|---|---|
    58	| English extraction against empty library | Same admission, quote, ladder, fiscal-period and identity checks; inspect all refusals. |
    59	| English updates against existing English library | Recall of the right thesis plus correct merge/repeat/replace/new decisions; chronology preserved. |
    60	| English-only API/UI | Same scores and numeric evaluations without Chinese fallback fields; complete bundles and source citations. |
    61	| Old ledger read | Same source IDs, evidence, dates and scores; no writes or bulk translation. |
    62	
    63	Prior decisions: D44 leaves question selection to the model without a count quota; D62 pins the provider/model; D63 sets daily judgement; D149 requires extraction-time association; D155 removes reference-list vetoes and defines identity checks; D159 establishes sequential extraction after writes; D162 failed and is not promoted; D163 selects English and a new ledger. These decisions are not changed by selecting a build population.
